<title>UK: European cotton trade hampered by holidays.</title>
<headline>European cotton trade hampered by holidays.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, ENGLAND 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>European cotton trade was hampered by many mills remaining closed for extended holidays over the Christmas and New Year period, brokers said.</p>
<p>However, a few new price monitoring enquiries were in evidence, notably in Portugal, Italy and Germany, although any business resulting from these was small, they added.</p>
<p>No noteworthy developments emerged from any eastern European markets.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8074</p>
